/-!
# N5.b (P6): N5 for every blowup step of the flattening algorithm

Lane G10N5, run 0081.  Hironaka 1975, p. 532 ("It is known that the ideal of the strict transform … is generated by
those elements `G^{-k} h` …"), in the exact native form consumed by lane G10GL (`G10HT/STATUS.md`):

* `presentation_geometric` — at every point of the geometric blowup `Bl_B X` over the centre, the native stalk map of
  the projection is a graph-chart presentation (canonical target data with `F := 𝟙 X`, the pivot cover of the target
  model open, `HironakaG10NfTargetPresentation.presentation_at`);
* `presentation_of_iso` — presentations transfer along an isomorphism over the base (BC3 `blowupIso`);
* `n5Holds_step` — N5 at every point of every step (off the centre: the generator is a unit,
  `HironakaG10NfPresentation.n5Holds_of_eq_top`);
* **`hN5`** — the native N5, with no hypotheses.

No named input.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open Set TopologicalSpace CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Hironaka.Analytic.Unibranch.HironakaG10NfN5

noncomputable section

